  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 104.48 Water quality control measures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 104.48 “Water quality control measures” means methods, practices, and devices that are designed and implemented to prevent or minimize erosion, siltation, or turbidity, or any combination thereof. The term includes but is not limited to phased construction, vegetated filter strips, geotextile silt fences, stormwater detention and infiltration systems, sediment detention basins, and any other method, practice, or device identified in Env-Wq 1506 through Env-Wq 1508.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 104.47)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
